.TH ZORG 1 2026-11-10 "zorg 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zorg \- a fast, lightweight, CLI-only Zcash wallet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zorg
.RI [ GLOBAL\ FLAGS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zorg
is a command-line Zcash wallet. It manages accounts, keeps a local
copy of the shielded blockchain state in a SQLite database, and builds
and broadcasts shielded transfers natively from the terminal.
zorg_index.db, each account's database, and the recovery phrases, encrypted
with a Secure Enclave identity per account, live in
.IR ~/.zorg/ .
The signed zorg.app build instead keeps the phrases in the macOS Keychain
and the databases in
.IR ~/Library/Application\ Support/zorg/ .
The two builds do not see each other's accounts.
zorg_index.db is the record of which accounts exist: each account's name,
network, and database path. It also holds the settings: the account the app
opens, whether it hides balances, and a server for testnet and for mainnet
that every command uses unless
.B --lwd
is given. Each account has its own database.
The database itself is not encrypted.
Running zorg without a command in a terminal shows the default account's
balance, syncing in the background, with a menu to send, receive, or see
history,
.B b
to hide or show balances,
.B s
for settings, until
.B q
or Esc quits; with no accounts it offers to create an
account or import a recovery phrase. Outside a terminal it lists accounts.
Names are case-sensitive and unique.
An account whose database is missing is reported as unavailable until
.B zorg accounts \-\-delete
removes it.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
Recognized before or after the command:
.TP
.BI \-\-network " main|test|regtest"
The new account's network, for create only. Defaults to mainnet.
.TP
.BI \-\-lwd " url"
lightwalletd endpoint override. Well-known public endpoints are the
default; use only if you need a specific one.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI zorg\ create " [name] \-\-new"
Create an account with a new recovery phrase in a new database and print
the phrase. Ask for a name if omitted. The wallet birthday is the current
chain tip (resolved via the lightwalletd endpoint) minus 100, rounded down to
a multiple of 100, and is printed with the address.
.TP
.BI zorg\ create " [name] \-\-import [\-\-birthday\ height]"
Create an account from an existing phrase, typed at a hidden prompt, at
derivation index 0 in a new database. Ask for a name if omitted. Reject a
phrase already known on the same network. Higher account-index discovery is
not implemented.
.IP
In a terminal, create asks which of the two when neither
.B \-\-new
nor
.B \-\-import
is given; without a terminal one is required. The new account becomes the
one the app opens.
.TP
.B zorg\ accounts
List all accounts across known databases. Each line shows the account
name, network, and unified address;
.B *
marks the account the app opens.
.TP
.BI zorg\ accounts\ \-\-rename " name " \-\-account " name"
Rename an account. The new name must be unique.
.TP
.BI zorg\ accounts\ \-\-default\ \-\-account " name"
Make the account the one the app opens.
.TP
.BI zorg\ accounts\ \-\-delete\ \-\-account " name"
Delete an account and its stored recovery phrase after a warning, Enter, and
Touch ID or the login password. Deleting an account deletes its database.
.TP
.BI zorg\ balance " [\-\-account\ name]"
Print spendable, pending, and locked balances for the account
(the only account, if none given; otherwise a name is required).
.TP
.BI zorg\ address " [\-\-new | \-\-transparent] [\-\-account\ name]"
Print the account's most recently used unified receiving address.
After restoring an account from its recovery phrase, this can be an address
that has already been paid; make a new one before handing it out.
With
.BR \-\-new ,
make a new address for the account and print it; the account must have been
synced first.
Every address the account has made keeps receiving.
With
.BR \-\-transparent ,
print the account's transparent address; funds received there stay
transparent until shielded.
.TP
.BI zorg\ address\ \-\-parse " address"
Print the receivers of a Zcash address.
.TP
.BI zorg\ sync " [\-\-account\ name]"
Sync every known database once, or the chosen account's database.
.TP
.BI zorg\ status " [\-\-account\ name]"
Print scan progress for every known database, or the chosen account's database.
.TP
.BI zorg\ send " to\ amount [\-\-memo\ text] [\-\-account\ name]"
Propose, authorize, and broadcast a shielded transfer of
.I amount
(ZEC on mainnet, TAZ on testnet)
to
.IR to .
Prints the fee before authorization and the broadcast txids after.
.TP
.BI zorg\ send " to " \-\-max\-amount " [\-\-memo\ text] [\-\-account\ name]"
Send all spendable shielded funds to
.IR to ,
minus the fee.
.TP
.BI zorg\ send\ \-\-shield " [\-\-account\ name]"
Move the account's transparent funds into its shielded balance.
.TP
.BI zorg\ history " [\-\-account\ name] [\-\-limit\ n]"
Print recent transactions.
.TP
.BI zorg\ tx " txid [\-\-account\ name]"
Print one transaction of the account in full: its amount and status, the
addresses it involves, its pool, fee, and memo.
.I txid
is written as
.B zorg history
and block explorers show it.
.TP
.BI zorg\ recovery " [\-\-account\ name]"
Print the account's recovery phrase and wallet birthday. Reading the
phrase asks for Touch ID or the login password.
